ransform={"rotate(142.5)"}></ellipse><ellipse pathlength={"1"} rx={"60"} ry={"19"} transform={"rotate(157.5)"}></ellipse><ellipse pathlength={"1"} rx={"60"} ry={"19"} transform={"rotate(172.5)"}></ellipse><circle pathlength={"1"} r={"34"}></circle><circle pathlength={"1"} r={"31.5"}></circle></svg></div></div></section><section id={"wl-ar-body"} className={"relative pb-(--section-space)"} aria-label={"The guide"}><div className={"container"}><figure className={"max-w-[60rem] mx-auto mb-[clamp(3rem,2rem_+_3vw,4.5rem)]"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><img className={"w-full aspect-video rounded-xl object-cover object-[var(--custom-pos,50%_50%)]"} src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1600x1600.svg"} alt={"A woman reading a letter at a table by a tall window"} width={"1600"} height={"1600"} decoding={"async"} style={{"--custom-pos": "50% 35%"}} /></figure><article className={"article-body article-body--flush custom-article-body"}><p className={"custom-article-first"}>{"Most families we meet worry about inheritance tax. Far fewer use the allowances that would shrink it. The rules aren't hidden — they're just easy to forget until the end of the tax year, when there's no time left to act."}</p><p>{"This checklist runs through what you can give away each year without any inheritance tax at all, in roughly the order we'd use them. None of it needs a trust or a solicitor. Most of it needs a diary note and a short conversation."}</p><h2>{"Start with the allowances you already have"}</h2><p>{"Everyone can give away £3,000 each tax year free of inheritance tax. If you didn't use last year's, you can carry it forward once — so a couple who missed last year could give £12,000 before 5 April."}</p><p>{"On top of that come the smaller exemptions, which add up faster than people expect."}</p><div className={"custom-checklist"}><p className={"custom-checklist-title"}><span className={"custom-rule-diamond"} aria-hidden={"true"}></span>{"Before 5 April"}</p><ul className={"custom-ticks grid gap-3.5"}><li><strong>{"Annual exemption:"}</strong>{" £3,000 each, plus last year's if unused."}</li><li><strong>{"Small gifts:"}</strong>{" up to £250 to as many people as you like."}</li><li><strong>{"Wedding gifts:"}</strong>{" £5,000 to a child, £2,500 to a grandchild."}</li><li><strong>{"Gifts from income:"}</strong>{" regular, from surplus income, with no limit."}</li><li><strong>{"Spouse or civil partner:"}</strong>{" gifts between you are exempt."}</li></ul></div><h2>{"The quiet power of gifts from income"}</h2><p>{"The least known exemption is often the most valuable. If you give regularly from income you don't need — not from savings — those gifts fall outside your estate straight away, however large they are."}</p><p>{"The test is simple to describe and important to record: the gifts must be regular, come from income, and leave you able to live as you normally do. A short note each year, kept with your will, does most of the work."}</p><blockquote className={"custom-article-quote"}><p>{"The best gifting plans aren't clever. "}<em>{"They're written down and repeated every year."}</em></p></blockquote><h2>{"The seven-year clock"}</h2><p>{"Larger gifts to people are usually free of inheritance tax if you live for seven years after making them. If you don't, and the gifts were above your £325,000 nil-rate band, the tax falls on a sliding scale."}</p><figure className={"custom-article-ledger"}><figcaption>{"Effective tax on a gift above the nil-rate band"}</figcaption><dl className={"custom-facts"}><div><dt>{"Within 3 years"}</dt><dd>{"40%"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"3 to 4 years"}</dt><dd>{"32%"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"4 to 5 years"}</dt><dd>{"24%"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"5 to 6 years"}</dt><dd>{"16%"}</dd></div><div><dt>{"6 to 7 years"}</dt><dd>{"8%"}</dd></div></dl></figure><p>{"That's why we often suggest giving earlier rather than later, and why a simple life policy written in trust can cover the tax for the seven years in between."}</p><figure className={"custom-article-figure"}><img src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/1400x1050.svg"} alt={"A quiet sitting room with a deep green sofa and a brass reading lamp"} width={"1400"} height={"1050"} loading={"lazy"} decoding={"async"} /><figcaption>{"A gifting plan works best when it's reviewed at the same time each year."}</figcaption></figure><h2>{"Pensions from April 2027"}</h2><p>{"Until now, most pensions have sat outside your estate. From April 2027, unused pensions are due to count towards it. For many families that reverses the old advice to spend other savings first and leave the pension untouched."}</p><p>{"If your plan relied on passing on a pension, it's worth a fresh look this year rather than next."}</p><h2>{"What to do this month"}</h2><ol><li>{"List the gifts you've made since last April, with dates."}</li><li>{"Check whether last year's £3,000 is still available to carry forward."}</li><li>{"Decide on any regular gifts from income, and start a simple record."}</li><li>{"Ask your adviser how the 2027 pension changes affect your plan."}</li></ol><p className={"custom-article-sign"}>{"— Tom Ashby, Bristol"}</p><p className={"text-[0.9375rem] text-muted custom-article-note"}>{"This guide is for general information and isn't personal advice. Tax rules can change, and their effect depends on your circumstances. The Financial Conduct Authority does not regulate tax or estate planning."}</p></article></div></section><section id={"wl-ar-author"} className={"relative pb-(--section-space)"} aria-labelledby={"wl-ar-author-name"}><div className={"container"}><aside className={"custom-card grid grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)] gap-7 max-w-[48rem] mx-auto sm:grid-cols-[auto_minmax(0,1fr)] sm:items-start"} data-anim={"fade-up"}><img className={"w-30 aspect-square rounded-full object-cover object-[50%_22%]"} src={"https://draftmango.com/draftmango/assets/media/placeholder/900x1200.svg"} alt={"Portrait of Tom Ashby"} width={"900"} heigh